sub:assertion {
<https://w3id.org/delphi/resource/claim/levin-2022-tame-05> a <https://w3id.org/delphi/ontology/Claim>;
    dc:description "Under TAME, how much agency a system has is an empirical, observer-dependent question: the correct level of agency to attribute is the one whose model and intervention strategy give the most efficient prediction and control of the system, as established by experiment.";
    dc:type "conceptual";
    <http://www.w3.org/2000/01/rdf-schema#label> "A system's level of agency must be determined empirically by prediction and control";
    <https://w3id.org/delphi/ontology/context> "Levin M, “Technological Approach to Mind Everywhere: An Experimentally-Grounded Framework for Understanding Diverse Bodies and Minds”, Frontiers in systems neuroscience (2022), doi:10.3389/fnsys.2022.768201; section “Technological Approach to Mind Everywhere: A Proposal for a Framework › Philosophical Foundations of an Approach to Diverse Intelligences”. Scope: Any living, engineered or hybrid system"
}
